---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="What is Life Care Planning? - Complete Guide"
  description="Learn what life care planning is, how it works, and why it matters. A comprehensive guide to life care plans for personal injury, medical malpractice, and disability cases."
>
  <Header />

  <main class="flex-1">
    <div class="page-container section-padding">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">What is Life Care Planning?</h1>

        <!-- Hero image -->
        <img
          src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1504813184591-01572f98c85f?w=1200&q=80&auto=format&fit=crop"
          alt="Medical professional reviewing a care plan with a patient"
          class="w-full aspect-video object-cover rounded-xl mb-8 shadow-sm"
        />

        <div class="prose prose-gray max-w-none">
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            Life Care Planning is a comprehensive approach to assessing and documenting the long-term 
            medical and support needs of individuals who have experienced catastrophic injuries, chronic 
            illnesses, or permanent disabilities.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">What is a Life Care Plan?</h2>
          <p>
            A Life Care Plan (LCP) is a detailed, comprehensive document that outlines the future medical 
            care, rehabilitation, support services, and associated costs for an individual throughout their 
            lifetime. It serves as a roadmap for the care and treatment that will be needed as a result of 
            an injury or medical condition.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">When is Life Care Planning Used?</h2>
          <ul class="space-y-2">
            <li><strong>Personal Injury Cases</strong> — Documenting future medical needs and costs after accidents</li>
            <li><strong>Medical Malpractice</strong> — Assessing long-term care requirements resulting from medical errors</li>
            <li><strong>Workers' Compensation</strong> — Determining ongoing medical support for workplace injuries</li>
            <li><strong>Divorce & Matrimonial</strong> — Evaluating long-term care costs for disabled spouses</li>
            <li><strong>Disability Cases</strong> — Supporting Social Security and VA disability claims</li>
          </ul>

          <img
            src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1589391886645-d51941baf7fb?w=1200&q=80&auto=format&fit=crop"
            alt="Legal documents and gavel representing personal injury cases"
            class="w-full aspect-video object-cover rounded-xl my-8 not-prose shadow-sm"
          />

          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">What Does a Life Care Plan Include?</h2>
          <ul class="space-y-2">
            <li>Projected medical treatments and procedures</li>
            <li>Rehabilitation services and therapy needs</li>
            <li>Medication and pharmaceutical requirements</li>
            <li>Home care and nursing assistance</li>
            <li>Adaptive equipment and assistive technology</li>
            <li>Transportation and accessibility modifications</li>
            <li>Cost projections and timeline estimates</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Why is Life Care Planning Important?</h2>
          <p>
            A well-prepared Life Care Plan provides objective, defensible documentation of future care needs 
            and costs. It helps attorneys, insurance companies, and courts understand the full scope of care 
            required, ensuring that individuals receive appropriate compensation and support for their 
            long-term needs.
          </p>

          <img
            src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1582750433449-648ed127bb54?w=1200&q=80&auto=format&fit=crop"
            alt="Care coordinator working with a patient and family"
            class="w-full aspect-video object-cover rounded-xl my-8 not-prose shadow-sm"
          />

          <!-- Video section -->
          <div class="not-prose my-8">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">Watch: Life Care Planning Explained</h2>
            <div class="rounded-xl overflow-hidden shadow-sm border border-gray-200">
              <iframe
                src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/6FsHeFMj_mQ"
                title="What is Life Care Planning?"
                allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture"
                allowfullscreen
                class="w-full aspect-video"
              ></iframe>
            </div>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 mt-2 text-center">Video placeholder — replace with client's YouTube video</p>
          </div>

          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-5">Common Questions</h2>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 not-prose mb-10">
            {[
              { q: "What guides life care planning?", a: "Plans are built on published standards of practice, clinical experience, and peer-reviewed guidelines — keeping recommendations consistent and grounded in accepted rehabilitation principles." },
              { q: "What makes a plan 'dynamic'?", a: "Life care plans can be updated as new assessments, treatments, or technologies emerge, keeping the roadmap aligned with current clinical realities rather than a single point in time." },
              { q: "How are costs calculated?", a: "Planners consider the full cost of each recommendation including frequency, replacement cycles, and maintenance — using regional cost data to keep projections realistic." },
              { q: "How often are plans updated?", a: "Updates are recommended whenever health status, available services, or relevant technologies change in meaningful ways to keep the document current and accurate." },
            ].map(item => (
              <div class="border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-5 bg-white">
                <p class="font-semibold text-brand-800 mb-2 text-sm">{item.q}</p>
                <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">{item.a}</p>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>

          <div class="mt-10 p-6 bg-brand-50 border border-brand-200 rounded-lg">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-brand-900 mb-2">Need a Life Care Planner?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">Browse our directory to find a qualified Life Care Planner in your state.</p>
            <a href="/locations" class="btn-primary text-sm">Find a Life Care Planner</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
